WEBVTT

00:45.045 --> 00:47.965
THE LEGEND OF KITCHEN SOLDIER

00:48.048 --> 00:52.427
SYSTEM OVERLOAD
SHUTTING DOWN SYSTEM

01:36.179 --> 01:37.598
Where am I?

01:50.819 --> 01:51.862
No way.

02:13.717 --> 02:15.344
EPISODE 4

02:20.599 --> 02:21.683
BASED ON THE WEBTOON SERIES THE LEGEND
OF KITCHEN SOLDIER BY ROBIN J, JIN-SU LEE

02:40.702 --> 02:41.745
You're here.

02:45.040 --> 02:47.459
- Dad.
- Oh, son.

02:47.793 --> 02:48.794
It's been a while.

02:57.094 --> 02:58.303
Oh, my.

02:59.471 --> 03:01.556
I thought you were all grown up,
going to the military.

03:01.640 --> 03:02.641
My goodness.

03:02.891 --> 03:03.892
Dad.

03:07.479 --> 03:08.772
How's military life treating you?

03:10.691 --> 03:12.943
I don't even know
how I get through each day.

03:13.235 --> 03:14.236
It's just that...

03:14.736 --> 03:16.947
there's never a quiet day.

03:17.280 --> 03:18.573
Is this how it's supposed to be?

03:19.658 --> 03:22.411
Well, it's tough when you're doing
something you've never done before.

03:22.994 --> 03:24.121
Do you remember that one time?

03:24.371 --> 03:25.956
I asked you to add some salt

03:26.039 --> 03:28.500
and you put in a ton of sugar
and ruined all the food.

03:30.001 --> 03:31.128
Did I do that?

03:31.211 --> 03:33.714
You'd make the ramyun all watery, too.

03:33.797 --> 03:35.298
And now you're a cook. My goodness.

03:35.632 --> 03:38.093
I can handle that much now.

03:38.176 --> 03:39.177
Right.

03:39.803 --> 03:42.139
At least I don't have to worry
about you starving somewhere.

03:42.431 --> 03:44.641
I still have a long way to go
to be like you, Dad.

03:45.809 --> 03:47.561
How did you get up so early every day

03:47.644 --> 03:50.147
to prep, cook, and clean the kitchen?

03:51.148 --> 03:52.399
Now that I've tried it myself

03:52.941 --> 03:53.942
it's truly amazing.

03:55.152 --> 03:56.570
The thing about cooking...

03:56.737 --> 03:58.280
If you think of it as a chore

03:58.363 --> 03:59.740
it becomes an endless chore.

04:00.449 --> 04:03.076
But when you see the happy faces
of people eating your food

04:03.326 --> 04:05.078
all those thoughts just disappear.

04:05.412 --> 04:06.997
Yeah, that feeling is
what keeps you going.

04:10.208 --> 04:11.209
Dad.

04:12.002 --> 04:13.003
I'm sorry.

04:16.673 --> 04:18.467
Every time I cook a meal...

04:20.427 --> 04:22.721
I think about how you worked
so hard your whole life

04:23.722 --> 04:25.098
and it just hits me.

04:28.518 --> 04:29.978
My son has really grown up.

04:30.604 --> 04:32.731
I can tell by how many things
you feel sorry about. My goodness.

04:52.501 --> 04:54.461
Son, if you only rely on your skill

04:54.544 --> 04:57.088
and overuse it, you won't improve.

04:58.131 --> 04:59.132
You knew all along?

04:59.508 --> 05:01.468
Getting cut by knives,
burning your hands...

05:01.676 --> 05:03.094
Carve those lessons onto your body

05:03.178 --> 05:05.096
to become a true chef. Understand?

05:12.395 --> 05:13.647
Slurp down this bowl.

05:14.147 --> 05:15.148
And...

05:16.233 --> 05:18.151
promise me you'll never
come back here again.

05:19.152 --> 05:20.320
What do you mean?

05:20.403 --> 05:21.696
Why shouldn't I come back?

05:21.780 --> 05:23.490
You punk. If you stay here

05:23.949 --> 05:26.368
what about your mom and Eun-jae,
who are waiting for you?

05:30.247 --> 05:32.833
You need to finish your quest
and live a better life than I did.

05:47.597 --> 05:48.598
Then...

05:51.685 --> 05:53.478
I'll try my best to live
just like you, Dad.

05:56.773 --> 05:57.774
There's no time.

05:57.858 --> 05:58.900
Hurry and drink.

06:05.365 --> 06:06.366
Hero.

06:06.449 --> 06:08.785
You have consumed
the Seaweed Soup of Resurrection.

06:09.786 --> 06:11.538
Would you like to reconnect?

06:16.585 --> 06:19.754
WOULD YOU LIKE TO RECONNECT?

06:48.199 --> 06:52.537
STAMINA

06:52.621 --> 06:54.915
Stamina has been fully recharged.

06:56.541 --> 06:57.542
Stamina?

07:00.420 --> 07:02.631
- Who's this guy?
- He's from the Ganglim Outpost.

07:02.714 --> 07:05.175
Well... they say he collapsed

07:05.258 --> 07:06.968
- while cooking, sir.
- Okay.

07:08.470 --> 07:09.930
Ah, crap. I'm out of hearts.

07:10.972 --> 07:12.223
Send me some hearts later.

07:12.307 --> 07:13.308
Yes, sir.

07:14.392 --> 07:16.061
- Kang Seong-jae?
- Private Kang Seong-jae.

07:16.144 --> 07:17.145
Does he have a fever?

07:17.228 --> 07:18.229
No, sir.

07:18.313 --> 07:19.356
Do you have any preexisting conditions?

07:19.439 --> 07:21.316
No, sir. I even got a
top grade on my physical.

07:21.399 --> 07:22.400
Oh, really?

07:22.484 --> 07:23.777
Everyone gets top grade,
even if they're sick.

07:24.444 --> 07:26.279
So what, you just suddenly collapsed?

07:26.529 --> 07:27.614
There must be a reason, right?

07:28.740 --> 07:29.741
Well...

07:29.824 --> 07:31.993
Warning. Stamina is low.

07:32.118 --> 07:33.828
If you do not rest immediately

07:33.995 --> 07:35.622
the system will shut down.

07:36.581 --> 07:37.999
- Oh, stamina...
- What?

07:41.503 --> 07:44.839
It says I'm low on stamina.

07:44.923 --> 07:45.924
Stamina?

07:46.967 --> 07:47.968
Damn it.

07:48.969 --> 07:51.179
Hey, I'm always low on that
because of guys like you.

07:52.222 --> 07:54.641
Why is everyone from Ganglim like this?

07:55.767 --> 07:56.768
Hey.

07:56.851 --> 07:58.144
If you're going to slack off, at least...

07:59.229 --> 08:01.272
Never mind. Good job. Very good.

08:01.606 --> 08:03.233
Hey, send one of those hearts
to this guy too.

08:03.566 --> 08:05.318
Okay? So he can go
with his stamina fully charged.

08:05.694 --> 08:07.320
- Yes, sir.
- Get some good rest.

08:09.572 --> 08:10.865
Jeez...

08:15.787 --> 08:17.414
For a dream...

08:19.249 --> 08:20.750
it felt incredibly real.

08:48.778 --> 08:50.488
Wait, Cho Ye-rin!

08:50.989 --> 08:52.490
Hey, long time no see.

08:53.116 --> 08:54.159
Hey I heard you're at Ganglim.

08:54.701 --> 08:55.702
That's rough.

08:58.079 --> 09:00.457
One of your guys is here.
Did you come to see him?

09:00.790 --> 09:02.292
Yes. How is he doing?

09:02.542 --> 09:03.835
What do you think?

09:03.918 --> 09:06.212
He's fine, but he collapsed for no reason.

09:06.296 --> 09:07.380
He's just faking it.

09:07.756 --> 09:08.882
If you ask me

09:08.965 --> 09:10.091
the vibe at Ganglim is just bad.

09:11.509 --> 09:13.636
I see army doctors practice
feng shui these days.

09:13.928 --> 09:16.014
I thought it had perfect feng shui.

09:17.891 --> 09:18.892
Must be nice.

09:19.809 --> 09:22.729
Then you can live there
happily ever after.

09:26.149 --> 09:27.150
Later.

09:35.950 --> 09:38.286
- Salute!
- So raising my level

09:38.912 --> 09:40.330
boosts stamina?

09:43.541 --> 09:44.793
So, as a noob

09:44.876 --> 09:46.920
I keep my head down
and grind for Experience Points?

09:50.006 --> 09:51.841
I've still got a long way to go.

09:54.719 --> 09:55.887
This is...

09:57.764 --> 09:58.765
Sa... salute!

10:00.683 --> 10:01.684
What were you doing?

10:02.560 --> 10:06.231
Oh, well...

10:06.356 --> 10:08.983
I thought I saw a fly
buzzing around, ma'am.

10:09.651 --> 10:13.196
A fly's been buzzing around for a while.

10:13.446 --> 10:15.156
They're bad to have in the hospital.

10:15.240 --> 10:17.033
For hygiene and all that.

10:17.534 --> 10:19.828
Gosh, this thing. Yes.

10:19.911 --> 10:21.621
COUNSELING OFFICE

10:26.835 --> 10:28.128
Are you really okay?

10:29.170 --> 10:30.588
Yes, I'm really fine, ma'am.

10:31.798 --> 10:34.259
I should have taken better care of myself.

10:34.676 --> 10:35.677
I apologize.

10:35.885 --> 10:37.804
Well, that's a relief...

10:38.555 --> 10:40.640
But I was worried
you were pushing through the pain.

10:40.932 --> 10:42.851
It's not because I'm sick or anything.

10:43.059 --> 10:44.060
I suppose...

10:44.310 --> 10:45.895
since the high-ranking officers
were coming

10:46.729 --> 10:48.439
I felt pressured to do well.

10:49.816 --> 10:52.735
I pushed myself to try
and make it extra delicious...

10:53.611 --> 10:55.280
but I guess I overdid it.

10:55.613 --> 10:56.990
You sure did.

10:57.198 --> 10:59.993
Everyone was making such a fuss,
asking if a private should do that.

11:02.036 --> 11:03.037
I'm sorry.

11:04.998 --> 11:05.999
Kang Seong-jae.

11:06.749 --> 11:10.003
Everyone's going crazy
asking what on earth the recipe is.

11:17.427 --> 11:19.220
It's a humble meal.

11:19.762 --> 11:21.598
I hope it's to the congressman's liking.

11:22.849 --> 11:24.976
Our soldiers work so hard.

11:25.393 --> 11:26.477
Instead of this...

11:26.561 --> 11:28.354
a bit more hearty meal

11:28.813 --> 11:32.108
like a whole chicken soup
would've been nice.

11:33.318 --> 11:36.070
You've come a long way to see
what our military's meals are like.

11:36.154 --> 11:38.573
So rather than a special dish
they rarely get to eat

11:38.656 --> 11:40.617
I thought it was right to serve you

11:40.700 --> 11:44.078
what our soldiers normally have.

11:44.913 --> 11:47.874
Still, with guests here,
you could've been more flexible.

11:50.585 --> 11:51.628
You little...

11:54.088 --> 11:55.089
Please, enjoy.

11:55.840 --> 11:56.841
Sure.

11:58.927 --> 12:00.011
Thank you.

12:01.012 --> 12:03.681
- Please, dig in.
- Enjoy your meal.

12:17.487 --> 12:19.197
Man, I can't watch this anymore.

12:31.334 --> 12:32.335
It's...

12:33.253 --> 12:34.254
It's...

12:35.505 --> 12:37.507
Congressman, are you all right?

12:37.590 --> 12:40.176
It's a thief!

12:40.260 --> 12:46.975
It's a thief!

13:00.780 --> 13:01.781
WANTED NOTICE

13:03.241 --> 13:04.951
The suspect is wanted for theft.

13:15.586 --> 13:16.587
Over there!

13:17.505 --> 13:18.965
Let's go, run!

13:41.029 --> 13:42.572
Finally caught you

13:42.655 --> 13:43.823
you thief!

14:11.851 --> 14:14.145
I can't stop eating this white rice.

14:14.604 --> 14:16.356
This dish is the real culprit.

14:16.439 --> 14:17.774
A rice thief!

14:18.232 --> 14:20.818
I guess you need to act like that
to get elected.

14:21.027 --> 14:23.321
I almost bought his act.

14:23.404 --> 14:25.573
He's such a pro at his eating show.

14:25.656 --> 14:26.824
The way his eyes lit up...

14:30.745 --> 14:32.497
The way you put it, Congressman

14:32.580 --> 14:33.748
now I'm curious too.

14:43.508 --> 14:48.137
Hey, you scoundrel!

14:57.355 --> 14:58.689
Stop right there!

15:00.024 --> 15:01.943
Stop! Give that back!

15:02.068 --> 15:04.195
Stop right there!

15:15.039 --> 15:17.625
Is it because the rice is so good?

15:17.875 --> 15:18.876
I can't stop eating.

15:18.960 --> 15:20.711
Is this Koshihikari or something?

15:20.795 --> 15:22.171
Or maybe Icheon rice?

15:22.463 --> 15:24.632
The rice is just the standard-issue
military kind.

15:26.050 --> 15:27.718
Then this must be the culprit!

15:27.802 --> 15:29.011
This braised pollack!

15:33.266 --> 15:34.267
I agree.

15:34.350 --> 15:36.352
It's my first time trying this
braised boneless pollack

15:36.436 --> 15:38.104
and it's divine.

15:41.357 --> 15:43.359
Hey! Can we get more rice?

15:43.443 --> 15:44.444
Rice!

15:44.527 --> 15:46.779
- Rice, rice, rice, rice.
- Rice, rice, rice, rice.

15:52.910 --> 15:54.412
What the hell are you doing?
We're swamped.

15:56.622 --> 15:57.665
Hey, Kang Seong-jae.

15:58.124 --> 15:59.125
Kang Seong-jae!

16:00.751 --> 16:01.752
BREAKING NEWS

16:02.378 --> 16:04.130
GETTING HIS FOURTH REFILL OF RICE
CONGRESSMAN KANG HONG-BEOM

16:04.213 --> 16:05.882
CHOMP, CHOMP

16:05.965 --> 16:07.008
YOU CHECKED THE MEAL CONTROVERSY, RIGHT?

16:07.091 --> 16:08.926
MORE

16:09.010 --> 16:10.636
ALL THAT WITH JUST BRAISED POLLACK?
HE CHOSE TO EAT THE SOLDIERS' FOOD...

16:10.720 --> 16:12.388
IF THE POLLACK MAKES HIM EAT
LIKE THAT, I'M CURIOUS...

16:12.513 --> 16:14.182
Certificate of Commendation.
By improving the meals

16:14.265 --> 16:16.267
This soldier has raised

16:16.392 --> 16:18.060
the image of army meals

16:18.144 --> 16:19.896
and boosted troop morale.

16:19.979 --> 16:21.022
He is presented with this award.

16:21.105 --> 16:23.900
Kim In-tae, 29th Division Commander.

16:28.738 --> 16:29.906
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun!

16:31.199 --> 16:34.118
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun,
seeing you work this hard to the end,

16:34.202 --> 16:36.579
The other soldiers should definitely
follow your example.

16:36.704 --> 16:38.581
My military service isn't over

16:38.664 --> 16:40.041
till it's over.

16:40.583 --> 16:42.919
Is that so? In that case,
I'll put you up for the NCO course

16:43.002 --> 16:44.545
so how about you give it some thought?

16:44.837 --> 16:47.381
You're too talented for us
to let you get discharged.

16:50.426 --> 16:52.053
Private Kang Seong-jae!

16:55.515 --> 16:57.517
Private Kang Seong-jae did well.

16:57.600 --> 16:59.143
That rice thief... I mean...

16:59.352 --> 17:02.230
Just thinking about that braised boneless
pollack is mouth-watering.

17:02.772 --> 17:04.190
Fresh, frozen, and dried pollack.

17:04.398 --> 17:07.360
Like a pollack, whose name changes
depending on how it's prepared

17:07.527 --> 17:09.111
it can become a delicious dish

17:09.195 --> 17:11.197
depending on whose hands cook it.

17:11.280 --> 17:12.406
You've shown that clearly.

17:12.949 --> 17:14.700
Private Kang Seong-jae!

17:14.784 --> 17:16.077
Until the day there are no more leftovers

17:16.160 --> 17:18.329
I will provide only delicious food
to my comrades.

17:18.621 --> 17:21.624
These soldiers will be awarded
a four-night, five-day leave.

17:21.707 --> 17:23.834
- Attention! Salute!
- Salute!

17:24.043 --> 17:25.044
Salute!

17:25.169 --> 17:28.714
You didn't serve a special meal,
but the regular menu the soldiers eat.

17:28.798 --> 17:30.758
I must say, that was a brilliant move.

17:30.967 --> 17:32.593
Was this Kang Seong-jae's idea too?

17:32.677 --> 17:34.428
- Private Kang Seong-jae.
- I'd say it was a team effort

17:34.512 --> 17:37.390
from our Ganglim Outpost.

17:37.765 --> 17:40.685
This really doesn't seem
like the Company Commander's plan.

17:41.185 --> 17:43.646
This bold approach is more
the Outpost Commander's style, no?

17:44.480 --> 17:45.523
No, sir.

17:45.606 --> 17:47.900
Private Kang suggested that
to approach it with sincerity

17:47.984 --> 17:49.777
we tackle it head-on with a menu

17:49.860 --> 17:52.321
infamous among those who've served.

17:54.073 --> 17:55.658
Why don't we just tackle this head-on?

17:55.741 --> 17:58.077
It's not like we can get our hands
on chicken right now...

17:58.828 --> 18:00.913
Wouldn't this seem more sincere, in a way?

18:02.164 --> 18:05.585
First Lieutenant Cho, I was worried
about your transfer to Ganglim

18:05.668 --> 18:07.878
but it's a relief to see
you're doing better than expected.

18:08.462 --> 18:10.339
You're starting to show some
real leadership qualities.

18:11.340 --> 18:12.550
- Thank you, sir.
- Of course.

18:13.593 --> 18:15.845
Before that, there is something
I'd like to propose.

18:16.470 --> 18:17.471
By all means.

18:20.266 --> 18:23.144
I think the problem with the meals is
not the soldiers who cook

18:23.227 --> 18:25.187
but lies within the supply chain process.

18:25.396 --> 18:27.106
Rather than inspecting
the state of the meals

18:27.189 --> 18:28.524
we need to investigate

18:28.608 --> 18:30.735
the supplier's food deliveries.

18:35.489 --> 18:39.160
Are you suggesting a problem with the
supplier, who was properly selected?

18:42.830 --> 18:43.831
Well...

18:47.752 --> 18:49.962
The eggs that were
delivered just yesterday

18:50.046 --> 18:51.255
were all spoiled.

18:52.256 --> 18:53.257
What?

18:55.134 --> 18:56.552
Spoiled eggs were delivered?

18:57.219 --> 18:58.804
Master Sergeant, did you know about this?

18:59.388 --> 19:02.099
No, sir. This is the first
I'm hearing of it.

19:02.183 --> 19:03.184
Private Kang Seong-jae

19:03.267 --> 19:06.062
you should've told the Company Commander.

19:06.687 --> 19:09.398
What if this had been discovered
when the congressman was visiting?

19:11.776 --> 19:15.488
I'll look into this matter
and make sure it's resolved

19:15.571 --> 19:16.906
so the Company Commander
and the Master Sergeant

19:17.114 --> 19:18.658
need to inspect everything thoroughly

19:18.741 --> 19:20.368
so this never happens again.

19:21.243 --> 19:23.204
- Yes, sir.
- How can you be so confident

19:23.287 --> 19:25.164
when you didn't know? What nerve.

19:28.834 --> 19:30.252
The men must have had a tough time.

19:30.336 --> 19:31.420
Arrange a company dinner for them.

19:32.505 --> 19:33.923
- A company dinner might be...
- Battalion Commander.

19:34.006 --> 19:35.883
I'll get the dinner arranged right away.

19:36.175 --> 19:37.176
Good.

19:37.927 --> 19:40.805
I can't remember the last time
we had a company dinner.

19:40.971 --> 19:43.307
We never had anything
good happen in Ganglim.

19:43.891 --> 19:45.101
Here, take this too.

19:47.645 --> 19:49.647
Well, look what we have here.

19:49.730 --> 19:51.649
This is the one everyone said
was too tacky to use.

19:51.732 --> 19:52.775
Hey.

19:52.858 --> 19:54.360
This is brand new. You want it?

19:54.902 --> 19:56.278
- Yes, sir.
- Go on, take it.

19:56.696 --> 19:58.989
- Thank you.
- It's finally found its owner.

19:59.448 --> 20:00.449
Let's go.

20:08.082 --> 20:09.458
ITEM

20:12.128 --> 20:14.004
You have acquired an item.

20:15.005 --> 20:17.174
ITEM

20:17.800 --> 20:19.510
When using the Rose-Knife item

20:19.593 --> 20:22.054
your cooking grade increases
by half a star.

20:22.138 --> 20:24.682
ROSE-KNIFE A-RANK
COOKING GRADE INCREASE

20:26.684 --> 20:27.685
Hey! Hey!

20:28.144 --> 20:31.188
This isn't the time to be all happy
just because you got a Rose-Knife.

20:32.106 --> 20:34.191
Still, a company dinner is
a good thing, isn't it?

20:35.192 --> 20:36.193
It's great.

20:36.402 --> 20:38.529
For everyone but us. Get it?

20:38.612 --> 20:39.613
Hey.

20:39.989 --> 20:41.949
Hurry up! What are you two doing?

20:42.032 --> 20:43.534
We're coming!

20:43.617 --> 20:44.785
- Hurry up.
- Yes, sir!

20:53.419 --> 20:54.879
- Man...
- Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

20:55.463 --> 20:56.630
Can you bring some more meat?

20:57.256 --> 20:59.175
The Battalion Commander
is running out of meat.

20:59.800 --> 21:00.968
Yes, sir. Right away.

21:01.385 --> 21:03.471
Kang Seong-jae, set these plates out.

21:03.804 --> 21:04.847
Yes, sir.

21:04.930 --> 21:05.931
Give that here.

21:06.265 --> 21:08.809
Good grief, would you look
at this rotten punk?

21:09.101 --> 21:11.771
I told you to grill the meat,
not turn it into charcoal.

21:12.229 --> 21:13.564
Just get out of the way.

21:13.647 --> 21:14.857
Good lord.

21:14.940 --> 21:17.651
You raised such a stink about
not getting enough meat

21:17.735 --> 21:19.528
and now there won't be any left
at this rate, you punk!

21:19.612 --> 21:21.864
It's a charcoal fire,
so the heat's hard to control, sir.

21:21.947 --> 21:23.199
Get it off the grill!

21:23.282 --> 21:25.075
Meat, meat, meat, meat.

21:25.659 --> 21:28.871
Hey, why is a cook struggling
to grill a piece of meat?

21:29.538 --> 21:30.539
Resting.

21:30.706 --> 21:32.333
It's called resting.
You lock in the juices

21:32.416 --> 21:34.668
so they explode, like "bam"!

21:34.919 --> 21:37.671
- Yes, sir.
- All this smoke is ridiculous.

21:38.923 --> 21:40.925
You're a Sergeant, and you can't
even grill meat properly.

21:41.550 --> 21:42.676
I'm very disappointed.

21:42.760 --> 21:43.761
Grill a new batch, now.

21:44.887 --> 21:46.639
- Gosh, the smoke.
- All that experience for nothing.

21:48.057 --> 21:49.391
Resting, my foot.

21:49.475 --> 21:51.644
The only "interesting" thing here is
that you're a Company Commander.

21:52.436 --> 21:54.814
Let's just think about my leave
and bear with it.

21:56.690 --> 21:57.817
You call this a company dinner?

21:58.067 --> 21:59.068
It's the Battalion Commander's
personal barbecue.

21:59.527 --> 22:01.445
As soon as the meat's cooked,
it goes straight to his table.

22:01.529 --> 22:03.072
Over food, of all things.

22:03.155 --> 22:04.949
So damn petty.

22:05.407 --> 22:06.408
Hey!

22:09.870 --> 22:11.914
- Private Kang Seong-jae.
- What are we, herbivores?

22:12.081 --> 22:13.123
Are we supposed to graze on grass?

22:13.582 --> 22:16.085
I'm sorry. But whenever I cook some,
the Company Commander takes it.

22:16.168 --> 22:19.505
Then you go tell him
to stop stuffing his face.

22:26.887 --> 22:30.474
Current soldiers' company dinner
satisfaction level is 35%.

22:30.683 --> 22:31.767
Are you okay?

22:34.436 --> 22:36.814
When feeling low, go for barbecue!

22:36.897 --> 22:38.858
Grill pork belly to raise

22:39.108 --> 22:41.360
the company dinner
satisfaction level to 80%.

22:42.945 --> 22:44.321
You'll gain Experience Points
if you succeed.

22:44.905 --> 22:47.700
But failure will lead to a random debuff.

22:51.537 --> 22:53.622
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun,
please go take a breather.

22:53.873 --> 22:55.416
I'll take over grilling.

22:55.791 --> 22:58.836
See? Who is this dinner even for?

22:59.128 --> 23:01.380
So stop giving them excuses
to throw these feasts.

23:01.714 --> 23:02.840
- Got it?
- Yes, sir.

23:08.012 --> 23:10.639
You have equipped the tongs item.

23:10.723 --> 23:11.724
ORDINARY TONGS
C-RANK

24:00.189 --> 24:02.900
Well, I'll be. Seong-jae knows
his way around a grill, doesn't he?

24:03.025 --> 24:05.611
He's flipping 'em with perfect timing.

24:05.778 --> 24:06.987
You know what I mean?

24:07.154 --> 24:09.865
Meat's no good if you keep
fussin' and flippin' it too much.

24:10.282 --> 24:11.784
You gotta do it just right.

24:11.867 --> 24:13.285
Just right, you know?

24:14.536 --> 24:15.579
- Yes, sir.
- Give it here.

24:17.122 --> 24:18.749
The fire's dying down.

24:18.832 --> 24:21.460
Then I can grill perfectly
when the heat's like this.

24:22.711 --> 24:23.921
It was too hot earlier.

24:24.505 --> 24:25.965
Hope you're eating while you're at it.

24:26.173 --> 24:27.174
Want me to help?

24:27.257 --> 24:28.384
Private Kang Seong-jae. No, ma'am.

24:28.467 --> 24:30.386
It's nice to see everyone having fun.

24:30.928 --> 24:31.929
What's nice about it?

24:32.012 --> 24:35.099
On the weekend, other soldiers get to rest

24:35.182 --> 24:37.267
but after this, when are we supposed
to clean up

24:37.351 --> 24:38.769
and get some rest?

24:38.852 --> 24:39.895
Hey, Outpost Commander.

24:40.396 --> 24:42.106
- Yes, sir.
- Come over and eat with us.

24:42.356 --> 24:43.691
Yes, sir. I'll be right there.

24:44.900 --> 24:45.901
Just hang in there.

24:46.235 --> 24:47.611
- I'm taking this.
- Yes, ma'am.

24:49.863 --> 24:50.864
I just need to get through this.

24:51.448 --> 24:52.658
My leave is coming up.

25:03.460 --> 25:05.004
All right, Kang Seong-jae.

25:06.338 --> 25:08.340
Oh, this piece right here.

25:08.424 --> 25:10.884
This balance of fat and lean meat...

25:10.968 --> 25:12.720
it's gotta be good ol' domestic pork.

25:13.429 --> 25:14.430
Master Sergeant.

25:14.972 --> 25:16.473
It's Ibérico.

25:16.557 --> 25:18.475
You know what that is, right?

25:18.767 --> 25:20.519
- Oh, yes.
- Pigs from the Iberian Peninsula in Spain

25:20.602 --> 25:21.770
raised on acorns.

25:21.854 --> 25:22.855
Hey, Company Commander.

25:22.938 --> 25:26.066
Just eat. Does it really matter?

25:26.150 --> 25:28.277
What's important is that
we're all eating together like this.

25:29.486 --> 25:31.238
Like I care where it's from.

25:31.321 --> 25:33.198
Meat is meat once it's in your mouth.

25:34.074 --> 25:35.075
Battalion Commander.

25:36.660 --> 25:39.121
I made this with love.

25:39.371 --> 25:40.372
Say "ah," sir.

25:41.331 --> 25:42.332
Whoa there.

25:42.416 --> 25:44.668
I don't accept love from other fellas.

25:48.589 --> 25:49.715
Hey, Lee Min-gu.

25:49.798 --> 25:50.799
Come over here.

25:53.302 --> 25:54.511
- Salute!
- Salute.

25:55.971 --> 25:58.015
That grilling meat smells incredible.

25:58.098 --> 25:59.391
- Here, have a seat.
- Yes, sir.

26:04.313 --> 26:07.316
He should join us
on a day like today. That's okay, right?

26:07.566 --> 26:10.152
Of course, sir. Why wouldn't it be okay?

26:10.235 --> 26:11.779
We're all one big family
in this battalion.

26:13.113 --> 26:14.198
Battalion Commander.

26:14.281 --> 26:16.408
I make a mean lettuce wrap.

26:16.492 --> 26:17.493
Oh, yeah?

26:17.576 --> 26:18.619
All right, let's see what you've got.

26:19.328 --> 26:21.163
Okay, prepare to be amazed.

26:27.461 --> 26:28.462
Battalion Commander.

26:47.481 --> 26:50.484
The fat isn't just chewy,
it's firm and springy.

26:51.235 --> 26:52.945
And the rich, savory flavor

26:53.028 --> 26:55.239
fills my mouth with every chew.

26:59.118 --> 27:00.119
Look at that.

27:00.202 --> 27:02.830
The big shots
always have the biggest reactions.

27:03.872 --> 27:06.041
It's just meat, for crying out loud.

27:07.459 --> 27:08.669
With these pickled greens...

27:09.253 --> 27:10.504
I should try some too.

27:28.480 --> 27:29.773
Oh my gosh!

27:30.023 --> 27:32.442
This is a total flavor bomb.

27:34.486 --> 27:38.490
It's throwing a whole party in my mouth.

27:42.995 --> 27:44.955
What a performance.

27:45.038 --> 27:47.708
Making a scene over one piece of meat.

28:22.117 --> 28:23.243
It's just meat...

28:28.332 --> 28:29.499
I mean, why...

28:30.500 --> 28:31.501
This dinner is for the soldiers.

28:31.585 --> 28:33.503
Shouldn't we head out?

28:37.841 --> 28:39.218
Is it that late already?

28:39.551 --> 28:41.762
Right, let's head out.

28:41.845 --> 28:43.222
Let's give the soldiers their time.

28:43.305 --> 28:45.390
But everyone's having such a good time.

28:45.933 --> 28:47.851
- What's the problem?
- Is this a proper dinner for them?

28:47.935 --> 28:50.562
The cooks haven't had a single bite
and are stuck just grilling.

28:53.899 --> 28:55.484
Well, since it's a shame to leave

28:55.859 --> 28:57.527
How about we get a drink after, just us?

28:57.903 --> 28:58.904
I'd love that.

28:59.154 --> 29:00.906
I have to do a gear inspection

29:00.989 --> 29:02.282
so I don't think I can make it.

29:02.366 --> 29:03.367
Oh, come on.

29:03.700 --> 29:06.411
When else will we get a chance
to talk over a drink?

29:10.332 --> 29:12.000
- Yes, sir.
- Good.

29:12.793 --> 29:14.211
- Let's clean up.
- Yes, sir.

29:17.506 --> 29:20.092
You have successfully achieved
Company Dinner Satisfaction.

29:22.844 --> 29:26.014
YOUR BEGINNER COOK LEVEL
HAS INCREASED

29:26.098 --> 29:27.557
Level up.

29:29.643 --> 29:31.395
The meal was great, thanks to you.

29:34.439 --> 29:36.066
Your grilling skills are no joke.

29:36.275 --> 29:37.651
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun!

29:39.278 --> 29:41.989
It was a great honor to grill
for the Battalion Commander...

29:42.072 --> 29:43.073
Private Kang Seong-jae.

29:43.407 --> 29:44.491
Private Kang Seong-jae!

29:44.741 --> 29:46.535
Can I look forward to this
again next time?

29:47.995 --> 29:50.205
I'll do my best
to live up to your expectations.

29:53.875 --> 29:54.876
All right. Let's go.

29:57.337 --> 29:59.589
At this rate, the Battalion Commander
is going to come here for every meal.

29:59.673 --> 30:01.508
He was absolutely beaming.

30:01.591 --> 30:04.052
At this rate, won't Kang Seong-jae
get poached for the Officers' Mess?

30:05.053 --> 30:06.596
What's different about the Officers' Mess?

30:06.805 --> 30:08.223
Dude, it's totally different.

30:08.307 --> 30:11.059
The cooks all have certifications

30:11.143 --> 30:13.895
and since it's for the top brass,
the ingredients are super fresh.

30:14.187 --> 30:15.188
It's a whole...

30:19.192 --> 30:20.193
But...

30:20.652 --> 30:22.195
I hear it's incredibly tough.

30:22.321 --> 30:24.656
Yeah, those dinners happen daily

30:24.740 --> 30:26.491
so they work till dawn. It's brutal.

30:26.616 --> 30:27.951
You get no sleep at all.

30:28.702 --> 30:29.703
Yeah.

30:30.203 --> 30:31.496
You have acquired the new keyword.

30:31.580 --> 30:33.707
Officers' Mess.

30:34.708 --> 30:35.709
Hey.

30:36.668 --> 30:37.669
Hey!

30:37.836 --> 30:38.837
Private Kang Seong-jae.

30:39.629 --> 30:42.507
Looks like you're getting ambitious
after a little praise

30:42.758 --> 30:45.302
but they don't take guys like us.

30:45.510 --> 30:46.511
Snap out of it!

31:09.743 --> 31:12.120
Even the carrots are pretty here,
Battalion Commander.

31:15.374 --> 31:16.875
This is kkanpung abalone

31:16.958 --> 31:20.128
made with premium abalone
in kkanpung sauce.

31:20.337 --> 31:22.589
- Enjoy your meal. Salute!
- Salute!00:31:23:16

31:24.674 --> 31:25.759
All right, everyone, dig in.

31:26.134 --> 31:27.135
This one...

31:27.427 --> 31:29.513
I picked out the plumpest one myself.

31:31.098 --> 31:32.099
Here you go.

31:39.481 --> 31:40.565
Where did it go?

31:40.982 --> 31:42.109
The abalone in my mouth...

31:42.275 --> 31:44.111
It just disappeared, Battalion Commander.

31:45.946 --> 31:48.156
Have you ever heard of that guy,
Lee Ho-young?

31:50.450 --> 31:51.952
The Ponte di Maestro Young Chef.

31:52.035 --> 31:53.954
A prodigy named one of Asia's Top Ten.

31:54.037 --> 31:56.164
Of course. Pongttedi Me...

31:56.748 --> 31:58.417
Yeah, it's famous. Pongttedi.

31:59.000 --> 32:00.460
With a chef like that cooking for me

32:00.544 --> 32:02.337
my standards are getting too high.

32:02.421 --> 32:04.131
How am I supposed to go back
to eating home-cooked food?

32:08.260 --> 32:09.594
Let me pour you a drink,
Battalion Commander.

32:13.598 --> 32:14.599
Here.

32:14.683 --> 32:15.725
Outpost Commander, have a drink.

32:16.560 --> 32:17.561
Thank you.

32:18.520 --> 32:21.231
Battalion HQ isn't the same
without our First Lieutenant Cho.

32:22.441 --> 32:23.817
You were a bit inexperienced at first

32:23.900 --> 32:25.485
but even then,
you had so much fighting spirit.

32:26.111 --> 32:27.112
Was I really?

32:27.863 --> 32:28.864
What's your take, Company Commander?

32:29.030 --> 32:30.031
Now that you've worked with her.

32:30.240 --> 32:32.033
Well, she still has a lot to learn

32:32.617 --> 32:34.536
so I've been training her diligently.

32:38.498 --> 32:41.001
What's so funny all of a sudden?

32:42.419 --> 32:43.420
It's just...

32:44.212 --> 32:45.922
I was wondering who's teaching who.

32:47.424 --> 32:48.592
You know about him, right,
Outpost Commander?

32:48.967 --> 32:51.678
Our Company Commander was a legend
at the Military Academy.

32:53.221 --> 32:54.598
He barely got in

32:54.681 --> 32:56.141
- and finished last.
- Min-gu.

32:56.308 --> 32:57.517
He was something else, in many ways.

32:57.601 --> 33:01.271
Why bring up ancient history, Min-gu?

33:01.480 --> 33:03.523
He's always like this,
Battalion Commander.

33:03.607 --> 33:06.359
He's still stuck in the past.

33:06.443 --> 33:08.778
He's right. Does that really matter?

33:09.112 --> 33:11.156
Our Company Commander
is doing a great job.

33:11.490 --> 33:12.991
The 4th Company's Ganglim Outpost

33:13.074 --> 33:14.284
is the hottest topic now, right?

33:14.367 --> 33:15.994
Oh, is that right?

33:16.286 --> 33:17.746
Thank you, Battalion Commander.

33:18.580 --> 33:21.041
You know, in all my years
in the military...

33:21.625 --> 33:24.419
Who'd have thought the mess hall food
would put us in the spotlight?

33:25.170 --> 33:26.421
So, on that note...

33:27.297 --> 33:30.050
I want to bring Private Kang Seong-jae
to the Officers' Mess.

33:32.761 --> 33:34.221
He's still a bit rough around the edges.

33:34.304 --> 33:36.681
But he can learn from his superiors
here and fill in the gaps.

33:37.015 --> 33:38.642
But the Officers' Mess...

33:38.975 --> 33:42.062
It's not a place you bring anyone, is it?

33:42.604 --> 33:43.980
He impressed high-ranking commanders

33:44.064 --> 33:46.525
and even the local congressman.

33:46.608 --> 33:48.902
What more does he have to do
to prove himself?

33:51.863 --> 33:54.324
If that's what you truly want,
Battalion Commander

33:54.574 --> 33:56.868
- I'll transfer Kang Seong-jae...
- No, sir.

33:59.371 --> 34:00.372
Hey, Cho Ye-rin.

34:00.664 --> 34:02.165
- You're interrupting the Commander...
- It's fine.

34:02.999 --> 34:04.417
Let's hear what the Outpost
Commander has to say.

34:06.086 --> 34:08.672
Private Kang Seong-jae
has been working on improving

34:08.755 --> 34:11.383
the Ganglim enlisted mess hall,
which was full of problems.

34:12.050 --> 34:14.261
But moving him to the Officers' Mess

34:15.345 --> 34:18.014
shows little consideration
for the soldiers at the outpost.

34:18.098 --> 34:20.809
I just want Private Kang Seong-jae
to be in a more flexible

34:20.892 --> 34:24.813
and better environment
where he can learn more.

34:27.983 --> 34:29.442
And if you're not satisfied with him...

34:30.402 --> 34:31.736
where will you send him next?

34:31.987 --> 34:33.029
Hey.

34:33.113 --> 34:35.532
If you're that drunk, go sleep it off.

34:36.157 --> 34:38.702
We didn't give you a voice
just for you to forget your place.

34:38.785 --> 34:39.786
No, it's okay.

34:40.161 --> 34:42.497
If she can't vent now, when will she?

34:44.457 --> 34:46.459
Outpost Commander,
it's been tough for you, hasn't it?

34:46.835 --> 34:48.587
I heard you relied on Major Im a lot.

34:50.797 --> 34:52.924
He may have been a good person to you

34:53.508 --> 34:55.385
but the very thought of him makes us sick.

34:55.468 --> 34:57.679
Because of that bastard,
several people nearly died.

34:57.762 --> 35:00.974
You used him all you could,
calling him a legendary top graduate

35:01.558 --> 35:04.686
You all pretended not to know him,
afraid you'd get burned too, right?

35:06.438 --> 35:09.274
- Hey, Cho Ye-rin!
- My transfer to the outpost

35:09.608 --> 35:12.861
can only be explained
by my closeness to Major Im.

35:13.820 --> 35:15.030
Hey, let's go.

35:16.156 --> 35:17.157
Sit down.

35:22.704 --> 35:24.289
Excuse me, I'm going to the restroom.

35:35.634 --> 35:37.052
I apologize, Battalion Commander.

35:37.427 --> 35:39.262
Officers who are about to be discharged...

35:40.263 --> 35:41.723
tend to get reckless.

36:17.717 --> 36:18.718
Are you upset?

36:29.562 --> 36:30.563
It's just...

36:31.189 --> 36:33.441
It's because I really want
to do a good job.

36:34.984 --> 36:37.153
No one can be perfect from the start.

36:38.488 --> 36:39.572
But weren't you...

36:39.989 --> 36:41.950
perfect from the start?

36:43.034 --> 36:44.869
No, I was a total disaster.

36:45.620 --> 36:46.621
But...

36:47.247 --> 36:50.125
if you truly trust yourself
and the people around you...

36:50.667 --> 36:52.460
the results will naturally follow.

36:54.045 --> 36:55.547
Easier said than done.

36:55.630 --> 36:57.090
You sound like Bob Ross or something.

36:57.841 --> 37:00.885
In time, you'll understand what I mean.

37:01.177 --> 37:04.013
Trusting someone isn't easy, you know.

37:05.014 --> 37:07.142
It takes a lot of courage.

37:09.853 --> 37:12.647
Ye-rin, I hope you never lose
that courage to trust people...

37:13.982 --> 37:15.108
until the very end.

37:23.616 --> 37:26.369
You thought you'd feel better
after saying your piece

37:27.120 --> 37:28.705
but I guess you still have more.

37:29.831 --> 37:31.499
Get your act together.

37:31.750 --> 37:33.376
Do you think this is the same
as some office job?

37:33.668 --> 37:36.254
Sure, you might be here
to just play soldier for a bit

37:36.671 --> 37:38.465
but for the rest of us,
our livelihoods are on the line.

37:39.966 --> 37:41.468
Please, try to read the room.

38:02.989 --> 38:03.990
Stop.

38:04.449 --> 38:05.450
Stop.

38:17.045 --> 38:18.046
All clear!

38:21.424 --> 38:22.717
Hey, Dong-hyun.

38:22.801 --> 38:24.344
You're sure full of energy today.

38:24.594 --> 38:27.013
At this rate, I could take on
the Special Forces!

38:27.096 --> 38:29.390
What's got our soldier boy
in such a good mood?

38:29.557 --> 38:31.226
I'm finally going on leave!

38:31.309 --> 38:32.894
Hey, that's great.

38:34.270 --> 38:36.856
I was wondering
when you'd finally get to go.

38:36.940 --> 38:39.651
Yoon Dong-hyun's finally on leave...
what a day.

38:39.734 --> 38:42.779
At this rate, I'll be discharged
before I know it.

38:44.656 --> 38:47.909
Once you're back from leave,
you'll be almost finished.

38:49.702 --> 38:51.371
Sir, this guy here...

38:51.663 --> 38:54.457
He keeps earning me commendation days
ever since he got here.

38:55.166 --> 38:57.126
My luck with new guys came too late.

38:57.210 --> 38:58.211
What a shame.

38:59.295 --> 39:00.505
Hurry up and take them.

39:07.887 --> 39:08.972
Whoa.

39:15.144 --> 39:17.397
The potatoes are in very poor condition.

39:17.981 --> 39:19.983
This may mean deductions in cooking.

39:20.066 --> 39:21.651
Please be advised.

39:23.611 --> 39:24.904
SEASONED LAVER
EXPIRING SOON

39:24.988 --> 39:27.282
PORK SPINE
UNDERWEIGHT

39:27.365 --> 39:29.284
CABBAGE
ORIGIN MISLABELED

39:29.367 --> 39:30.410
FROZEN POLLACK
NOT FRESH

39:30.493 --> 39:32.161
PORK BELLY
UNDERWEIGHT, EXPIRING SOON

39:34.289 --> 39:35.331
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

39:35.415 --> 39:37.000
These potatoes have sprouted.

39:37.083 --> 39:38.793
Should we accept them like this?

39:38.960 --> 39:41.337
Come on, just cut that part out.
It won't kill you.

39:47.677 --> 39:50.138
If we sweat the small stuff,
it just makes things harder for us.

39:50.221 --> 39:53.474
Is leaving out some onions
really going to make a difference?

39:53.558 --> 39:55.351
Oh no, it fell.

39:56.060 --> 39:57.687
What, is there a problem?

40:00.106 --> 40:01.983
The rations are in poor condition, sir.

40:02.567 --> 40:04.319
It's fine, okay?

40:04.527 --> 40:05.820
You know how it is.

40:05.904 --> 40:07.488
It's from all the rain this summer.

40:07.655 --> 40:09.073
It's fine. I checked everything.

40:09.157 --> 40:12.243
Even people go crazy in the summer.
We have to be understanding.

40:12.327 --> 40:14.037
It's fine. Okay?

40:16.539 --> 40:17.540
Salute!

40:17.999 --> 40:19.876
Still, if there's a problem,
we need to fix it.

40:21.085 --> 40:23.671
Why are you doing the inspection
instead of the Master Sergeant?

40:24.005 --> 40:25.798
Are enlisted soldiers supposed
to do the inspection?

40:26.299 --> 40:28.760
Well, normally a superior is supposed
to be here with us.

40:33.348 --> 40:36.309
It says here each box should weigh 10kg...

40:38.728 --> 40:40.146
Is that right?

40:40.229 --> 40:41.230
I don't think so.

40:41.522 --> 40:43.983
Hey, why are you being so difficult
all of a sudden?

40:44.317 --> 40:46.402
Sir! If the supplier changed

40:46.486 --> 40:48.446
shouldn't the quality
of the ration be better?

40:49.489 --> 40:52.158
Hey, I worked my butt off
to meet your budget, okay?

40:52.241 --> 40:55.453
I've been working my tail off
since dawn without any sleep.

40:55.745 --> 40:57.997
We're not running a restaurant here.

40:58.081 --> 40:59.082
What's the big deal?

40:59.165 --> 41:01.459
This won't do.
I was going to let it slide.

41:02.335 --> 41:04.796
But I will be reporting this
to my superiors.

41:05.505 --> 41:06.965
What, you're going to report this?

41:09.884 --> 41:11.761
Fine, do whatever you want! Damn it.

41:13.429 --> 41:15.348
Hey, get out of the way! Take the picture.

41:15.431 --> 41:17.558
RATION RECEIPT INSPECTION SHEET

41:20.019 --> 41:21.854
The inspections haven't been
at all logged recently.

41:22.772 --> 41:25.817
The Master Sergeant or Deputy
Outpost Commander should check it.

41:25.900 --> 41:27.694
But they couldn't care less.

41:27.860 --> 41:29.821
Then you should have told me.

41:29.904 --> 41:30.905
I'm sorry.

41:31.906 --> 41:33.491
- Yoon Dong-hyun.
- Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

41:33.574 --> 41:36.536
I know you're excited about your award
and your final leave

41:36.744 --> 41:38.246
but let's stick to the basics.

41:38.663 --> 41:40.331
- Yes, ma'am.
- Kang Seong-jae.

41:40.707 --> 41:41.916
Private Kang Seong-jae.

41:42.000 --> 41:44.502
If you wanted this job so badly,
then see it through to the end.

41:44.585 --> 41:47.088
Don't cut corners
and try to muddle through.

41:48.214 --> 41:49.215
Yes, I understand.

41:54.679 --> 41:56.222
LIKEABILITY

41:56.305 --> 41:57.932
LIKEABILITY 10%

41:59.308 --> 42:00.643
- Salute!
- Salute!

42:05.273 --> 42:08.359
I don't know why our Outpost Commander
makes things so difficult.

42:08.568 --> 42:11.487
Honestly, aren't we both just waiting
to get out of here?

42:11.696 --> 42:13.865
Still, the state of the ingredients today

42:13.948 --> 42:15.491
really crossed a line.

42:15.575 --> 42:18.911
What good is calling it out now?
You saw what happened before, right?

42:18.995 --> 42:21.789
Our Company Commander only cares
about the egg for his own ramyun

42:21.873 --> 42:25.001
he doesn't give a damn about the eggs
rotting away in the fridge.

42:25.334 --> 42:26.961
So what's the bottom line? Never forget.

42:27.086 --> 42:28.546
Our true enemy...

42:29.047 --> 42:30.089
is the officers.

43:04.332 --> 43:06.125
GOLDEN WAGON

43:06.209 --> 43:07.877
This is the outpost situation room.

43:08.127 --> 43:10.379
The Golden Wagon has now arrived.

43:10.463 --> 43:13.633
I repeat, the Golden Wagon
has now arrived.

43:13.716 --> 43:15.676
Oh, come on. Make some sense.

43:16.385 --> 43:17.887
You obviously bet on Liverpool.

43:17.970 --> 43:19.722
Why would you bet on Manchester United?

43:20.723 --> 43:22.642
You were totally blinded by the payout.

43:23.184 --> 43:25.019
Man, that's why you always
lose all your money.

43:27.855 --> 43:29.190
Whatever, I'm hanging up.

43:29.899 --> 43:32.652
I need to sell a lot this time...

43:34.028 --> 43:36.197
All right. Bye.

43:36.280 --> 43:37.573
Open for business!

43:41.536 --> 43:42.537
What?

43:43.037 --> 43:45.289
These guys usually go nuts
when the Golden Wagon arrives.

43:45.373 --> 43:46.374
Why is it so quiet?

43:46.457 --> 43:48.209
VIGILANCE IS OUR MISSION

43:50.419 --> 43:51.420
Yeah?

43:53.464 --> 43:54.465
One shampoo, please.

43:55.550 --> 43:56.551
Is that all?

43:56.968 --> 43:57.969
Really?

43:58.302 --> 43:59.303
Do I have to buy more?

43:59.470 --> 44:03.224
Hey, kid, you go crazy for
chocolate cookies and potato chips.

44:04.475 --> 44:05.685
I'm not in the mood today.

44:11.566 --> 44:13.025
- Here.
- Thank you.

44:16.696 --> 44:19.490
What's with these guys acting so weird?

44:19.782 --> 44:20.950
I won't even make enough to cover gas.

44:21.742 --> 44:23.286
Ko Tae-seok.

44:23.369 --> 44:25.246
- Get me some smokes.
- Sergeant.

44:25.621 --> 44:26.831
Yeah, and put the cost on the...

44:26.914 --> 44:28.332
- you know, the tab.
- Sure.

44:28.916 --> 44:31.210
But it feels like
there isn't a soul at the outpsot.

44:31.294 --> 44:32.295
Did something happen?

44:32.545 --> 44:33.546
Happen?

44:33.838 --> 44:34.881
What's there to happen?

44:38.384 --> 44:41.137
Business is slow, so Ko Tae-seok here
is getting all worked up.

44:41.470 --> 44:45.016
Ganglim is my biggest gold mine,
that's why I'm asking.

44:45.558 --> 44:49.437
For the past few months,
sales here have been really sweet.

44:49.645 --> 44:51.606
That's not going to happen for a while.

44:52.732 --> 44:53.733
Huh? What?

44:54.817 --> 44:57.153
Try the mess hall if you're curious.

44:58.154 --> 44:59.155
The mess hall?

45:01.616 --> 45:02.992
It's really delicious, isn't it?

45:08.623 --> 45:10.625
If there's any food left,
give him a plate.

45:10.708 --> 45:11.876
Yes, right away.

45:13.711 --> 45:15.504
- Go on, eat up.
- Yes, sir.

45:21.385 --> 45:22.678
Enjoy your meal.

45:26.682 --> 45:27.683
Jeez.

45:28.267 --> 45:30.019
This is just regular old army food.

45:30.186 --> 45:32.855
And they're acting like
this is going to ruin my business.

45:32.939 --> 45:34.106
What a joke.

45:45.993 --> 45:47.828
You used the Rose-Knife item.

45:47.912 --> 45:50.623
A bonus half-star has been added.

45:50.706 --> 45:52.041
ACORN JELLY SALAD
THE CHEWY TEXTURE IS ON POINT!

45:54.961 --> 45:56.796
You used the Rose-Knife item.

45:56.879 --> 45:59.590
A bonus half-star has been added.

45:59.674 --> 46:00.883
PORK SPINE POTATO STEW
IT'S GOT A NICE KICK!

46:01.259 --> 46:03.344
GANGLIM UTD, FC GOLDEN WAGON

46:03.427 --> 46:04.804
He's going. He keeps going.

46:04.887 --> 46:06.180
He's not stopping.

46:06.264 --> 46:07.890
Yes, Ko Tae-seok is fantastic.

46:07.974 --> 46:10.351
He's leaving all defenders behind.

46:10.434 --> 46:11.602
Now it's one-on-one with the goalie.

46:11.978 --> 46:13.396
And now he shoots!

46:39.046 --> 46:40.047
What is this?

46:40.298 --> 46:41.757
He's absolutely helpless

46:41.841 --> 46:44.010
against the pork backbone.

46:45.011 --> 46:46.012
Look at his form.

46:46.095 --> 46:47.555
How high can his leg go?

46:47.638 --> 46:48.973
A scorpion kick?

46:49.348 --> 46:51.392
With a ridiculous angle

46:51.475 --> 46:53.519
Ko Tae-seok prepares his special move.

47:00.276 --> 47:02.695
No matter how good it is,
it's just army food!

47:03.821 --> 47:04.822
And he shoots!

47:05.781 --> 47:07.325
Will it find the back of the net?

47:07.408 --> 47:09.327
- Will it?
- Will it?

47:09.744 --> 47:11.078
He takes the shot!

47:23.632 --> 47:26.802
Will it go in?

47:27.261 --> 47:30.014
In the end,
he can't get past the acorn jelly.

47:32.600 --> 47:35.561
GANGLIM 1 - 0 GOLDEN WAGON

48:05.174 --> 48:07.343
It totally kills any desire to snack.

48:08.094 --> 48:09.678
It was an excellent meal.

48:14.558 --> 48:16.811
What in the world

48:16.894 --> 48:19.397
have you been doing to my pigs!

48:19.772 --> 48:22.608
When they see your slop bucket

48:22.691 --> 48:23.984
they act like they've been starved.

48:24.068 --> 48:26.320
They just go absolutely wild for it.

48:32.660 --> 48:33.786
This means...

48:34.328 --> 48:37.832
you must have put something in the food.

48:52.680 --> 48:54.682
That's why the little fellas...

48:55.266 --> 48:56.767
are going nuts.

49:01.021 --> 49:02.231
Level up!

49:09.864 --> 49:10.865
Good morning.

49:11.115 --> 49:12.491
- Good morning.
- What the...

49:12.575 --> 49:13.784
- Good morning.
- Why did I...

49:14.326 --> 49:15.369
sleep so well?

49:18.622 --> 49:21.333
PROFICIENCY
BASIC KNIFE SKILLS LEVEL 3

49:26.255 --> 49:28.591
Begin calisthenics!

49:28.674 --> 49:30.634
- One, two, three, four
- One, two, three, four

49:30.718 --> 49:33.304
- five, six, seven, eight.
- five, six, seven, eight.

49:33.387 --> 49:36.182
- One, two, three, four
- One, two, three, four

49:36.265 --> 49:39.226
- five, six, seven, eight.
- five, six, seven, eight.

49:41.687 --> 49:43.105
PROFICIENCY
BASIC KNIFE SKILLS LEVEL 4

49:48.944 --> 49:50.863
All right, almost there.

49:51.822 --> 49:53.032
- Last lap.
- Switch!

49:55.367 --> 49:56.494
Switch! You punks.

49:56.911 --> 49:57.912
Let's go!

49:58.913 --> 50:00.039
What the heck?

50:00.623 --> 50:01.624
Are they all elite soldiers or what?

50:01.707 --> 50:03.584
Stop running! I said, stop running!

50:04.251 --> 50:06.045
It's over! Stop running!

50:07.087 --> 50:09.423
PROFICIENCY
BASIC KNIFE SKILLS LEVEL 5

50:21.727 --> 50:24.355
DAILY QUEST: SLICING CARROTS 10/10
REWARD: 100 EXPERIENCE POINTS

50:24.438 --> 50:27.024
You have completed the daily quest.

50:34.198 --> 50:35.783
Hey, you busy?

50:35.866 --> 50:38.911
What do you mean, "why"?
Dude, Yoon Dong-hyun is back!

50:38.994 --> 50:40.996
I'm going on leave,
so clear your schedule.

50:41.080 --> 50:42.790
Yeah.

50:44.750 --> 50:46.210
You have an exam coming up?

50:48.546 --> 50:50.130
Right. Okay, I get it.

50:50.422 --> 50:51.465
All right.

50:52.007 --> 50:53.008
Bye.

50:54.843 --> 50:56.679
Hey, where are you? It's Dong-hyun.

50:57.054 --> 50:58.222
Hey, I'm going on leave next week.

50:58.305 --> 51:00.516
We've gotta celebrate, right?

51:02.184 --> 51:04.186
Oh, you have a date with your girlfriend.

51:04.687 --> 51:06.105
Yeah. Got it.

51:06.188 --> 51:07.439
I'll call you. Okay.

51:07.523 --> 51:09.108
Okay, bye.

51:12.528 --> 51:13.529
Hi, Mom.

51:13.612 --> 51:14.905
I'm going on leave next week.

51:14.989 --> 51:15.990
Yeah.

51:17.199 --> 51:18.617
You're going on a trip to Europe.

51:19.243 --> 51:20.244
Right.

51:21.245 --> 51:22.913
Yeah, got it. Okay.

51:22.997 --> 51:24.790
Yeah, I'll call you. Okay.

51:27.126 --> 51:29.211
Looks like they've gotten much closer
while I've been away.

51:39.763 --> 51:41.932
I'm used to the Outpost Commander
acting like that.

51:42.016 --> 51:44.268
Day in and day out,
it's "inspection, inspection."

51:44.685 --> 51:45.894
"How old are the onions?"

51:45.978 --> 51:47.605
"Have the potatoes sprouted or not?"

51:47.688 --> 51:49.773
She's a total critic.
A professional critic.

51:50.024 --> 51:52.192
What's the point of good ingredients

51:52.276 --> 51:53.694
if Dong-hyun gets his hands on them?

51:53.777 --> 51:55.988
- It becomes worse than dog food.
- Hey.

51:56.196 --> 51:59.408
Hey, don't go poking the bear.
He's almost done.

51:59.658 --> 52:01.410
Once Yoon Dong-hyun is on leave

52:01.493 --> 52:02.911
Kang Seong-jae will take over.

52:03.203 --> 52:05.914
Would Dong-hyun even know
what to tell Seong-jae to do?

52:07.249 --> 52:09.376
I mean, honestly,
about that reward leave he got...

52:09.460 --> 52:11.795
Didn't he get it all by riding
the New Recruit's coattails?

52:11.879 --> 52:13.255
That's enough.

52:14.798 --> 52:16.550
But isn't it strange?

52:16.634 --> 52:18.677
Ever since Kang Seong-jae got here

52:18.802 --> 52:20.888
the whole vibe at the outpost
has somehow changed.

52:20.971 --> 52:23.599
Maybe it's because our food
has gotten better, don't you think?

52:23.682 --> 52:26.644
It's true. Better food on the table
definitely improves the mood.

52:26.727 --> 52:29.480
- You can say that again.
- Oh, that Kang Seong-jae.

52:29.772 --> 52:32.024
Yoon Dong-hyun is such a leech.

52:32.107 --> 52:33.692
Way to go, Kang Seong-jae!

52:33.776 --> 52:35.778
Jeez, Yoon Dong-hyun
always leeching off him like that.

52:56.924 --> 52:59.176
Daily Quest has been completed.

52:59.259 --> 53:00.928
Acquiring Experience Points.

53:06.141 --> 53:08.018
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun,
I can finish that.

53:08.394 --> 53:09.395
I got it.

53:10.771 --> 53:11.814
I'll finish it in a second.

53:11.897 --> 53:13.565
I said I'll do it!

53:18.654 --> 53:20.114
LIKEABILITY

53:20.197 --> 53:21.740
LIKEABILITY 70%

53:22.950 --> 53:24.618
Kang Seong-jae.

53:24.702 --> 53:26.245
Company Commander is looking for you.

53:27.705 --> 53:29.873
Hey, you just walk in
without saluting now?

53:32.084 --> 53:33.085
Salute.

53:33.168 --> 53:34.211
I'm here to get Seong-jae.

53:34.294 --> 53:36.130
The Armed Forces TV
wants to do an interview.

53:36.672 --> 53:38.966
What? From Armed Forces TV?

53:39.049 --> 53:41.135
Well, look at the war hero.

53:41.385 --> 53:42.636
Hurry up and go, kid.

53:44.430 --> 53:45.556
I'll be back.

54:00.320 --> 54:01.864
Because of all the visitors
for Kang Seong-jae

54:01.947 --> 54:03.407
I can't get any rest, damn it.

54:03.490 --> 54:05.159
Aren't we just playing second fiddle

54:05.242 --> 54:07.244
at the Kang Seong-jae festival?

54:07.327 --> 54:09.037
Just think of it as part of our duty.

54:09.121 --> 54:11.165
Don't get twisted up and complain.

54:11.582 --> 54:12.666
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

54:13.167 --> 54:14.418
- Do it properly.
- Yes, sir.

54:18.672 --> 54:19.798
What's with Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun?

54:19.882 --> 54:21.759
He'd been all smiles about his leave.

54:22.509 --> 54:24.136
I'm not really sure.

54:24.720 --> 54:26.221
How can you not know?

54:26.305 --> 54:28.390
If a mess hall mood carries over

54:28.474 --> 54:30.017
don't you know it makes things hard
for the rest of us?

54:31.810 --> 54:32.811
I know.

54:33.395 --> 54:34.396
Kang Seong-jae!

55:26.740 --> 55:28.534
You've lost so much weight.

55:29.535 --> 55:30.536
Are you okay?

55:30.744 --> 55:31.745
Are you having a tough time?

55:36.208 --> 55:38.377
Goddamn...

55:43.215 --> 55:45.634
SPECIAL THANKS TO
PARK MYUNG-HOON FOR HIS APPEARANCE

56:06.446 --> 56:08.866
THE LEGEND OF KITCHEN SOLDIER

56:09.074 --> 56:12.619
Reporting! I'm on my first leave,
effective today.

56:12.703 --> 56:15.080
- You've worked hard.
- But...

56:15.789 --> 56:17.332
aren't there too few customers?

56:17.416 --> 56:19.084
You have left the designated
military area.

56:19.167 --> 56:21.003
Skill usage is restricted.

56:21.461 --> 56:23.338
The wait is at least two hours here.

56:23.422 --> 56:25.090
You will now begin eating.

56:25.173 --> 56:26.258
- Let's eat!
- Let's eat!

56:26.341 --> 56:27.843
How is the flavor so deep?

56:28.719 --> 56:32.764
I'll prove the mess hall runs fine
without Kang Seong-jae.

56:34.141 --> 56:35.559
I would like to learn from you.

56:36.059 --> 56:38.937
Can you really do whatever it takes?
